{
  "_doc": [
    "Interest tiers for acquisition surveys (#7294). Read by scripts/audit/candidate-tier-survey.ts.",
    "A = core (alchemy, Hermetica, Kabbalah, Rosicrucianism, magic/grimoires, mysticism/theosophy, astrology).",
    "B = adjacent (early modern science & medicine, natural philosophy, books of secrets, emblem books, first vernacular translations of classical/patristic/oriental works).",
    "C = everything else public domain (pre-1900). Nothing is filtered OUT by these lists; they only rank.",
    "Each entry is a JavaScript regex SOURCE, matched case-insensitively against the title + subjects (+ author for *_authors), after Unicode NFD and stripping combining marks (so write 'bohme', not 'böhme'). Use \\b only where the word boundary is in Latin script.",
    "'universal' applies to every language (Latin titles turn up in every national catalogue). Per-language lists are keyed by the canonical language name the survey emits.",
    "Edit this file and re-run the survey; do not hard-code terms in the script.",
    "'search_terms' are the same tiers as word stems for a SOURCE's own search box (Europeana, Delpher, Polona, BVPB…), where a regex cannot run: they give the per-source tier estimates in library-harvest-registry.md. Keep them in step with the regex lists."
  ],
